{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unromantic-ferny-arawana","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe duration investigation reconstructed end-to-end `review-plan` and gated-close wall time from Codex rollout logs and tracker sidecars using a temporary read-only probe. The operator asked that this probe live under the project `scripts/` directory for reuse. The temporary version contains machine-specific paths and snapshot bounds, so the repository version must expose those as inputs while preserving the frozen analysis defaults through explicit command arguments.\n\n## Plan\n- Add `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py` as a read-only CLI that links top-level Codex shell invocations through yielded cells and PTY polls, resolves ticket aliases, matches model-backed gate sidecars, and reports end-to-end percentiles.\n- Make log roots, tracker directory, time bounds, provider filter, and recent-regime cutoff configurable; use repository-neutral defaults where safe.\n- Add a gated-close phase breakdown using directly observed tracker event timestamps and clearly label inferred residual time.\n- Add focused tests for command classification, terminal reconstruction, percentile calculation, and close-phase decomposition without reading the live tracker or user session logs.\n- Document script usage in its module help text; do not change agent-duration guidance in this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The reusable probe is stored at `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py` without hard-coded user-home or worktree paths.\n- [ ] CLI arguments can reproduce the frozen analysis window and select current-regime cohorts.\n- [ ] No-LLM, forced, status/check/help, unmatched, and interrupted operations remain distinguishable from completed model-backed cohorts.\n- [ ] Gated-close output separates pre-verifier residual, deterministic verifier, LLM verifier, verdict-to-status, status-to-signature, and remaining post-write tail when evidence is available.\n- [ ] Inferred phases are explicitly labeled and do not claim unsupported direct instrumentation.\n- [ ] Focused tests pass using synthetic fixtures only.\n- [ ] Repository guidance is not updated until the operator separately confirms duration wording.","id":"2bcd-4c47-6f05-4605","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["metrics","tooling","agent-telemetry"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Persist reusable gate-duration probe"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787526911721222001,"uuid":"f71122a2-b618-49ab-a9e8-65ee644ec232"}